      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey, my company just sent me this new \"ergonomic\" high-end office chair for my home setup... idk something feels off about it. it's way too heavy and it feels like it's reacting to me when i sit down. i'm pretty sure there's some kind of biometric sensor in the lumbar support or the seat pan to track my vitals or something. i dont want them tracking my stress levels or focus while i work. do u know any ways i can mask my biological signals or disrupt sensors while i'm sitting in it?",
